  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/100) by Sebastien Guyader (Bitbucket: [Sebastien Guyader](https://bitbucket.org/Sebastien Guyader), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nWhen I open a raw in the editor, with neutral profile, the colors are strange. As it uses the automatched color profile, I tried “camera standard” \\(weird colors too\\) and “no profile \\(no weird colors\\). It happens with several raw formats \\(RAF, CR2, NEF\\).\n\nBelow a screen shot with “automatched profile” left, and “no profile” right:\n\n![](https://bitbucket.org/repo/9pArXyE/images/745021653-2020-06-02_19-10.jpg)\nBuild info:\n\nVersion: 1.3-104-gfe2b315b8  \nBranch: master  \nCommit: fe2b315b8  \nCommit date: 2020-06-02  \nCompiler: cc 10.1.0  \nProcessor: x86\\_64  \nSystem: Linux  \nBit depth: 64 bits  \nGtkmm: V3.24.2  \nLensfun: V0.3.95.0  \nExiv2: V0.27.2  \nBuild type: Release  \nBuild flags: -mptwrite -std=c\\+\\+11 -march=native -Werror=unused-label -fno-math-errno -flto -Wall -Wuninitialized -Wno-deprecated-declarations -Wno-unused-result -fopenmp -Werror=unknown-pragmas -O3 -DNDEBUG -ftree-vectorize  \nLink flags:  -march=native -flto  \nOpenMP support: ON  \nMMAP support: OFF  \nBuild OS: Linux  \nBuild date: 2020-06-02T23:28:23Z\n",
